    "explanation": "Recognize transistor type\nThe arrow points FROM the center line TOWARD terminal P, indicating an NPN transistor.\nStep 3: Identify terminals\nIn a transistor symbol:\n\nBASE (B): The line that connects to the central vertical bar (terminal Q)\nCOLLECTOR (C): The line without an arrow (terminal R)\nEMITTER (E): The line with the arrow (terminal P)\nThe arrow always points from emitter, indicating current flow direction.\n\nP = EMITTER (has arrow)\nQ = BASE (center connection)\nR = COLLECTOR (top terminal without arrow)\n\nP, Q, R represent: EMITTER, BASE and COLLECTOR"
