    "explanation": "Original length, L₀ = 20 m\nInitial temperature, T₁ = 25°C\nFinal temperature, T₂ = 75°C\nLinear expansivity, α = 2.0 × 10⁻⁵ K⁻¹\nGap required = ?\n\nSolution:\nStep 1: Calculate temperature change\nΔT = T₂ - T₁\nΔT = 75 - 25\nΔT = 50°C = 50 K\nStep 2: Apply linear expansion formula\nFormula: ΔL = αL₀ΔT\nWhere:\n\nΔL = change in length (expansion)\nα = linear expansivity\nL₀ = original length\nΔT = temperature change\n\nStep 3: Substitute values\nΔL = 2.0 × 10⁻⁵ × 20 × 50\nΔL = 2.0 × 10⁻⁵ × 1000\nΔL = 2.0 × 10⁻²\nΔL = 0.02 m\nStep 4: Interpretation\nThe gap must accommodate the expansion of the metal rod when temperature increases from 25°C to 75°C.\nGap required = 0.02 m"
