    "explanation": "Given information:\nObject height, h₀ = 4 cm\nObject distance, u = 15 cm\nFocal length, f = 5 cm (positive for concave mirror in Cartesian sign convention)\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Mirror formula\n1/f = 1/u + 1/v\n1/5 = 1/15 + 1/v\n\nStep 2: Solve for image distance v\n1/v = 1/5 – 1/15 = 3/15 – 1/15 = 2/15\nv = 15/2 = 7.5 cm\n\nStep 3: Magnification formula\nMagnification m = v / u = 7.5 / 15 = 0.5\nAlso, m = image height / object height = hᵢ / h₀\n\nStep 4: Find image height\nhᵢ = m × h₀ = 0.5 × 4 cm = 2 cm"
