    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nHeight (h) = 20 meters\nInitial velocity (u) = 0 m/s (ball is released, not thrown)\nAcceleration due to gravity (g) = 10 m/s²\nTime (t) = ?\n\nUsing the equation of motion:\nh = ut + ½gt²\nSince u = 0 (released from rest):\nh = ½gt²\nRearranging to find t:\nt² = 2h/g\nt = √(2h/g)\nSubstituting values:\nt = √(2 × 20/10)\nt = √(40/10)\nt = √4\nt = 2 seconds\nAnswer: A. 2 sec"
