    "explanation": "Given information:\nIn water: fraction submerged = 50% = 0.5\nIn glycerine: fraction submerged = 40% = 0.4\nDensity of water, ρ_w = 1000 kg m⁻³\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Density of the sphere from water data\nFor a floating object, the fraction submerged equals the ratio of the object's density to the fluid's density.\nρ_sphere / ρ_w = fraction submerged in water\nρ_sphere / 1000 = 0.5\nρ_sphere = 500 kg m⁻³\n\nStep 2: Use glycerine data to find its density\nρ_sphere / ρ_g = fraction submerged in glycerine\n500 / ρ_g = 0.4\nρ_g = 500 / 0.4 = 1250 kg m⁻³"
