    "explanation": "Given information:\nDC voltage that produces the same brightness, V_dc = 12 V\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Condition for equal brightness\nFor a resistive load like a lamp, brightness depends on the power dissipated.\nEqual brightness means equal power delivered to the lamp.\n\nStep 2: Power comparison\nFor DC: Power P_dc = V_dc² / R\nFor AC: Power P_ac = V_rms² / R\n\nStep 3: Equate powers\nV_rms² / R = V_dc² / R\nV_rms = V_dc\n\nStep 4: Substitute value\nV_rms = 12 V"
