    "explanation": "I. Melting: Solid to liquid transition; molecules gain energy to overcome fixed positions, showing molecular motion and interactions.\n\nII. Boiling: Liquid to gas transition; molecules gain enough energy to break intermolecular forces, demonstrating molecular kinetic energy and forces.\n\nIV. Conduction: Heat transfer via molecular collisions (or electron movement), directly showing molecular motion and energy transfer.                           Melting, boiling, and conduction are direct evidence of the molecular nature of matter."
