    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nThickness of rod (d) = 0.02 m\nTemperature at hot junction (T₁) = 80°C\nTemperature at cold junction (T₂) = 20°C\nTemperature gradient = ?\n\nFormula for temperature gradient:\nTemperature gradient = Change in temperature / Distance\nTemperature gradient = ΔT / d\nStep 1: Calculate temperature difference\nΔT = T₁ - T₂\nΔT = 80 - 20 = 60°C = 60 K\nStep 2: Calculate temperature gradient\nTemperature gradient = 60 / 0.02\nTemperature gradient = 3000 K/m\nTemperature gradient = 3.0 × 10³ Km⁻¹"
