    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nOriginal length (L₀) = 4 m\nExtension₁ (e₁) = 0.02 m\nMass = 0.4 kg, so Force₁ (F₁) = 0.4 × 10 = 4 N (assuming g = 10 m/s²)\nApplied force₂ (F₂) = 15 N\nFinal length = ?\n\nUsing Hooke's Law:\nExtension is proportional to applied force (for elastic materials):\nF ∝ e\nSetting up proportion:\nF₁/e₁ = F₂/e₂\nSolving for e₂:\n4/0.02 = 15/e₂\ne₂ = (15 × 0.02)/4\ne₂ = 0.30/4\ne₂ = 0.075 m\nCalculate final length:\nFinal length = Original length + Extension\nFinal length = 4 + 0.075\nFinal length = 4.075 m ≈ 4.08 m"
