    "explanation": "Given information:\nInitial nuclide: ²¹⁰₈₂Pb (mass number 210, atomic number 82)\nFinal nuclide: ²⁰⁶₈₀Pb (mass number 206, atomic number 80)\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Determine changes in mass and atomic numbers\nChange in mass number = 210 – 206 = 4\nChange in atomic number = 82 – 80 = 2\n\nStep 2: Identify particle(s) that produce these changes\n\nAn alpha particle (⁴₂He) decreases mass number by 4 and atomic number by 2.\n\nA beta particle (⁰₋₁e) increases atomic number by 1 with no mass change.\n\nStep 3: Match the changes\nA single alpha emission exactly accounts for:\nΔA = –4, ΔZ = –2\nThis matches the observed changes. No beta particle is involved."
