    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nMillivoltmeter maximum reading = 10 mV\nTemperature difference (0°C to 100°C) produces 4 mV\nReference junction at 0°C\nMaximum temperature = ?\n\nStep 1: Find the temperature-voltage relationship\nTemperature difference of 100°C produces 4 mV\nRate = 100°C / 4 mV = 25°C per mV\nStep 2: Calculate maximum temperature\nMaximum reading = 10 mV\nMaximum temperature difference from 0°C:\nΔT = 10 mV × 25°C/mV = 250°C\nMaximum temperature:\nT_max = 0°C + 250°C = 250°C"
