    "correctAnswer": "C",
    "explanation": "Given information:\nInitial velocity, u = 30 m/s\nDistance to traffic light, s = 50 m\nFinal velocity at light, v = 0 m/s\n\nStep 1: Use kinematic equation for constant acceleration\nv² = u² + 2 a s\n\nStep 2: Substitute known values\n0² = 30² + 2 × a × 50\n0 = 900 + 100 a\n\nStep 3: Solve for deceleration a\n100 a = –900\na = –9 m/s²\n\nThe magnitude of deceleration is 9 m/s²."
