    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nRelative density of gold = 19.2\nMass of gold, m = 2.4 kg\nVolume, V = ?\n\nSolution:\nStep 1: Understand relative density\nRelative density (specific gravity) = Density of substance / Density of water\nDensity of water = 1000 kgm⁻³\nStep 2: Calculate density of gold\nDensity of gold = Relative density × Density of water\nρ = 19.2 × 1000\nρ = 19,200 kgm⁻³\nStep 3: Apply density formula\nFormula: Density = Mass/Volume\nρ = m/V\nStep 4: Rearrange for volume\nV = m/ρ\nStep 5: Substitute values\nV = 2.4/19,200\nV = 0.000125 m³\nV = 1.25 × 10⁻⁴ m³"
