    "correctAnswer": "C",
    "explanation": "Given information:\nWave equation: y = a sin(150πt - (π/4)x)\nPhase difference Δφ = 45° = π/4 rad\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Identify the wave number\nComparing with standard form y = a sin(ωt - kx):\nWave number k = π/4\n\nStep 2: Phase difference formula\nFor a progressive wave, phase difference Δφ = kΔx\nHere Δx is the distance x we want to find.\n\nStep 3: Substitute values\nπ/4 = (π/4) * x\n\nStep 4: Solve for x\nx = (π/4) / (π/4) = 1"
