    "explanation": "Given information:\nEach cell: e.m.f = 1. V, internal resistance r = 2.5 Ω\nThree cells connected as shown.\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Interpret the diagram\nThe diagram indicates a parallel connection of the three cells. In a parallel combination of identical cells, the net e.m.f is the same as that of one cell, and the internal resistance is the parallel combination of the individual internal resistances.\n\nStep 2: Calculate net e.m.f\nFor cells in parallel, net e.m.f E = 1.5 V.\n\nStep 3: Calculate net internal resistance\nFor identical resistors in parallel:\n1/R = 1/r + 1/r + 1/r = 3/r\nR = r/3 = 2.5 Ω / 3 ≈ 0.833 Ω"
