    "id": "physics-1788729141052-293-784",
    "questionText": "During the nuclear reaction described by\n²³⁵₉₂W → ²³⁵₉₃X → ²³¹₉₁Y\nthe particles emitted are respectively (JAMB 2007)",
    "options": [
      "α and α",
      "α and β",
      "β and β",
      "β and α"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "explanation": "Analyzing the nuclear reactions:\nFirst reaction: ²³⁵₉₂W → ²³⁵₉₃X\nChange in mass number (A): 235 → 235 (no change)\nChange in atomic number (Z): 92 → 93 (increase by 1)\nParticle emitted:\n\nMass number unchanged\nAtomic number increases by 1\nThis indicates β⁻ (beta) decay\n⁰₋₁β or electron emission\nA neutron converts to proton: n → p + e⁻\n\nSecond reaction: ²³⁵₉₃X → ²³¹₉₁Y\nChange in mass number (A): 235 → 231 (decrease by 4)\nChange in atomic number (Z): 93 → 91 (decrease by 2)\nParticle emitted:\n\nMass number decreases by 4\nAtomic number decreases by 2\nThis indicates α (alpha) decay\n⁴₂He or helium nucleus emission\n\nSummary:\n\nFirst emission: β (beta particle)\nSecond emission: α (alpha particle)"
