    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nMass (m) = 2 kg\nVelocity (v) = 10 m/s\nRadius (r) = 4 m\nCentripetal force (F) = ?\n\nFormula for centripetal force:\nF = mv²/r\nSubstituting values:\nF = (2 × 10²)/4\nF = (2 × 100)/4\nF = 200/4\nF = 50 N.  This centripetal force of 50 N is directed towards the center of the circular path and is necessary to keep the 2 kg object moving in a circle at 10 m/s. This force must be provided by friction, tension, gravity, or some other physical force depending on the situation (e.g., tension in a string, friction on a road, etc.)."
