    "correctAnswer": "C",
    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nInitial length (L₁) = 0.4 m\nInitial period (T₁) = 2 s\nNew length (L₂) = 0.8 m\nNew period (T₂) = ?\nSame location (same g)\n\nFormula for period of simple pendulum:\nT = 2π√(L/g)\nKey relationship:\nT ∝ √L (period is proportional to square root of length)\nMethod 1: Using ratio\nT₁/T₂ = √(L₁/L₂)\nRearranging:\nT₂ = T₁ × √(L₂/L₁)\nSubstituting values:\nT₂ = 2 × √(0.8/0.4)\nT₂ = 2 × √2\nT₂ = 2√2 s"
