    "explanation": "Given information:\nMass, m = 20 kg\nHeight, h = 10 m\nAcceleration due to gravity, g = 10 m s⁻² (assumed)\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Energy conservation principle\nWhen the object falls from rest, its initial potential energy is converted entirely into kinetic energy just before hitting the ground (ignoring air resistance).\n\nStep 2: Calculate potential energy at the top\nPotential energy, PE = m × g × h = 20 kg × 10 m s⁻² × 10 m = 2000 J\n\nStep 3: Kinetic energy just before impact\nBy conservation of energy, KE just before impact = PE at top = 2000 J"
