    "explanation": "Given information:\nRadius of Earth, R = 6.4 × 10⁶ m\nAcceleration due to gravity, g ≈ 9.8 m s⁻² (standard value, though not explicitly given, it is implied for such problems)\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Formula for escape velocity\nEscape velocity, vₑ = √(2gR)\n\nStep 2: Substitute the values\nvₑ = √(2 × 9.8 × 6.4 × 10⁶)\nvₑ = √(2 × 9.8 × 6.4 × 10⁶) = √(125.44 × 10⁶) = √(1.2544 × 10⁸)\n\nStep 3: Calculate\n√(1.2544 × 10⁸) = 1.12 × 10⁴ m s⁻¹ = 11.2 km s⁻¹ ≈ 11.3 km s⁻¹\n\nFinal Answer:\nThe escape velocity is approximately 11.3 km s⁻¹."
