    "explanation": "Understanding cell types:\nPrimary cells:\n\nNon-rechargeable (disposable)\nExamples: dry cells, alkaline batteries\nRelatively high internal resistance\nCannot produce large currents for long periods\nChemical reactions are irreversible\n\nSecondary cells:\n\nRechargeable\nExamples: lead-acid batteries, lithium-ion batteries\nLow internal resistance\nCan deliver large currents for extended periods\nChemical reactions are reversible\n\nSecondary (rechargeable) cells have very low internal resistance, which allows them to deliver large currents efficiently."
