    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nPower (P) = 30 W\nTemperature rise (ΔT) = 10°C = 10 K\nTime (t) = 5 minutes = 5 × 60 = 300 seconds\nHeat capacity (C) = ?\n\nStep 1: Calculate total heat energy supplied\nEnergy = Power × Time\nQ = P × t\nQ = 30 × 300\nQ = 9000 J\nStep 2: Calculate heat capacity\nHeat capacity is the heat required to raise the temperature by 1K:\nQ = CΔT\nRearranging for C:\nC = Q/ΔT\nSubstituting values:\nC = 9000/10\nC = 900 JK⁻¹"
