    "explanation": "Given information:\nMass of ice, m = 90 g\nDensity of ice, ρᵢ = 0.9 g/cm³\nDensity of water, ρ_w = 1.0 g/cm³\n\nSolution:\n\nStep 1: Calculate initial volume of ice\nVᵢ = m / ρᵢ = 90 / 0.9 = 100 cm³\n\nStep 2: Calculate final volume of water (after melting)\nV_w = m / ρ_w = 90 / 1.0 = 90 cm³\n\nStep 3: Calculate change in volume\nΔV = V_w – Vᵢ = 90 – 100 = –10 cm³\nThe negative sign indicates a decrease in volume. The magnitude of change is 10 cm³."
