    "explanation": "Given information:\n\nMoon's gravity, gₘ = (1/6)gₑ\nMass of bowling ball remains constant\nWeight on moon = ?\n\nSolution:\nStep 1: Define weight\nWeight = mass × acceleration due to gravity\nW = mg\nStep 2: Calculate weight on Earth\nWₑ = mgₑ\nStep 3: Calculate weight on Moon\nWₘ = mgₘ\nWₘ = m × (gₑ/6)\nWₘ = (1/6)mgₑ\nWₘ = (1/6)Wₑ\nStep 4: Compare weights\nWeight on moon = (1/6) × Weight on Earth"
